Earlier we observed that only the GSU Burndown alert was resolving labels correctly, while the other alerts (Spillover and HTTP error alerts) were returning null values for project and model variables. Later today we also noticed that the Burndown alert stopped resolving the project name when using ${metric.label.resource_container}. After further testing, we found that using ${resource.project} successfully resolves the project name from the monitored resource metadata. With this change, the Burndown alert now works correctly again and displays the project name. The Spillover and HTTP error alerts now show the project name as well, but the model name (model_user_id) is still not resolving, so investigation is ongoing to determine the correct variable mapping for the model label.
